From 7b53643cbaa7d79f899845e7400a6c5289537460 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:42:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] resolve: a `use` of another crate's tuple struct leaves out a constructor
 it can't name

swash 0.2.7 (agg 1.9.0) src/internal/var.rs:247, in `pub fn adjust_axis(.., coord: Fixed) -> Option<Fixed>`
(the module's own `use super::fixed::Fixed`, a `pub struct Fixed(pub i32)`):
    use skrifa::raw::{tables::avar::Avar, types::Fixed, FontData, FontRead};
    Some(Fixed(mapping.apply(Fixed::from_bits(coord.0)).to_bits()))
= "<null> error:0: Type mismatch between swash::internal::fixed::Fixed and font_types::fixed::Fixed".

font_types 0.11.3 declares `pub struct Fixed(i32)` (private field) in a private module and re-exports it with
`pub use fixed::{.., Fixed}`. rustc gives a tuple struct's constructor the narrowest of the struct's and its
fields' visibilities, and import resolution treats a binding the importing module can't access as absent in that
namespace: the body-local `use` imports only the TYPE `Fixed` (so `Fixed::from_bits` is font_types'), and the call
`Fixed(..)` resolves further out to swash's own constructor. mrustc imported font_types' constructor too.

Both places that bind another crate's constructor at the end of an import chain now skip it unless every field is
`pub` (the HIR keeps per-field publicity): Resolve_Use_GetBinding (use.cpp, a single `use`) and the HIR glob in
Resolve_Index_Module_Wildcard__glob_in_hir_mod (index.cpp). Not covered: the same rule for a crate's own items
(AST side), and `#[non_exhaustive]` structs (their constructor is `pub(crate)`; the HIR doesn't record the
attribute).

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

